menu "Neo2 Buddy Configuration"

config SUPPORT_BATTERY
    bool "Enable battery support"
    default y
    help
      Enable voltage sensing and battery percentage reporting. When disabled
      battery-related code and UI features will be omitted.

config SUPPORT_SDCARD
    bool "Enable microSD card support"
    default y
    help
      Enable mounting and use of an external microSD card. When disabled the
      SD mount attempts are omitted and only internal flash storage is used.

config SUPPORT_OLED
    bool "Enable 1.3in OLED status display"
    default y
    help
      Build with OLED support for a small on-device status display. When
      disabled only the web UI will be available for status and control.

config BUDDY_RUN_SELF_TEST
    bool "Run boot self-test suite"
    default y
    help
      Run lightweight smoke tests once at boot and log results to the
      device log buffer. Disable to shorten boot time after validation.

config BUDDY_UART_CMD
    bool "Enable protected UART command console"
    default y
    help
      Start an interactive command line on the serial port (115200). Use
      "login <password>" (same as the web portal) before Neo USB commands.
      Intended for development and automated testing over the CH340 UART.

endmenu
